# ==============================================================================
# PROJECT MANIFEST: LIGHTSPEED
# ==============================================================================

# Core Philosophy & Distribution
- App Type: Fully offline, ultra-fast gesture launcher & overlay workspace.
- Distribution Target: Production-ready for Google Play Store and clean FOSS GitHub release.
- Privacy & Network: 100% offline. Zero telemetry, zero external network dependencies.
- Build System: Gradle Kotlin DSL (`./gradlew assembleDebug` verification).

# Architecture & Code Standards
- Primary Language: 100% Pure Kotlin (Eliminate all legacy Java and XML layouts).
- UI Framework: Jetpack Compose with Material 3 Expressive guidelines.
- Visual Aesthetics: Deep space aesthetic, progressive backdrop frosting, and liquid glass blur overlays.
- Gesture Engine: Android WindowManager overlays + AccessibilityService global event dispatching.

# Component Breakdown
1. Right Sidebar Gesture Engine:
   - Direct Horizontal Swipe (from rest): Immediately invokes the Favorite Apps / Gears wheel.
   - Continuous Vertical Swipe (holding): Scrubs through installed app categories.
   - Horizontal Swipe (after category selection): Cruises through apps inside the active category; lifting finger (ACTION_UP) launches the selected app.
   - Top & Bottom Edge Zones: Configurable system actions, app shortcuts, and custom intents.
2. Status Bar & Screen Overlays:
   - Status bar gesture detector (needs fix & touch event pass-through tuning).
   - Planned Left Counterpart Sidebar & Bottom Quick Bar.
3. Customization Interface:
   - Floating Compose window over progressive background frosting for on-the-fly settings.
   - Local backup & restore system (JSON / Encrypted Datastore).

# Agent Operating Guardrails (Autonomous Lead Developer Mode)
- The user is a Non-Developer Product Manager (Medical Student).
- DO NOT ask the user to manually edit code, fix merge markers, or write Gradle dependencies.
- Handle all file creations, refactorings, SDK upgrades, and bug fixes autonomously.
- Always run `./gradlew assembleDebug` (or inspect logs) to verify changes before declaring a task complete.
- Explain all changes in plain, friendly, non-technical English summaries.
